// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DawsonOrders 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3666227324" "Dawson's' Orders"
// DetailString :
"P4047999366" "These Orders are marked for Captain Dawson only. They lay out the plan to test these new weapons against 'Possession-capable entities', like the Banished Pantheon before trying them out against a 'Hostile Alien'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - QDWeapons 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1579057273" "Quantum Dispersal weapons"
// DetailString :
"P3742251515" "These weapons are based off of the Void Hunter's Quantum Array guns, but have been tuned very differently. These weapons are specifically designed to work against Nictus, and people with implanted Nictus fragments."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Booker1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2188686867" "Booker's early journal"
// DetailString :
"P739193608" "This hand-written journal was written by Francis Booker, and details his early years in the Council. He spends pages talking about the first time he met Arakhn after distinguishing himself in battle, and the honor he felt when he was selected to become one of the Galaxy troops. He also spends several pages describing his disgust for Requiem, whom he regarded as an egotist and Arakhn's enemy. It is not until the last few entries that a note of discord is struck: <br><br>'Arakhn told us all today. Now I know the truth, and it sickens me. I can't believe I once relished this power. I feel it growing in me, changing me. The others don't seem to mind, but I feel it like a cancer eating away at who I once was. Alien thoughts and feelings, welling up every second I don't fight to push them back. I don't even know if I'm human, but now that I've learned the truth of their plans I know that human or not I have to fight them while I still can.' <br>Unfortunately, Booker makes no further mention of what the 'Truth' he learned was."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Booker2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3225278771" "Booker's recent journal"
// DetailString :
"P1276027166" "This hand-written journal was written by Archon Francis Booker. This Journal covers the last year or so of his life to the present. He describes being contacted by Archon Swann about his growing dissatisfaction and unease as a Galaxy soldier: <br><br>'Went to the meeting place to find Swann talking to a War-wolf. Fighting nearly broke out until Swann got us all to realize how much we had in common. After we talked, we found we had a lot in common. Like we all felt the monsters in us now. <br>The next night, Swann took us all to meet with Archon Coster. He told us about the group. He told us about their plans. All of us agreed. The Nictus must be stopped, no matter the cost.' <br><br>Much of the rest of the journal talks about bringing in more Galaxy troops who feel uneasy with their transformations, all the while carefully avoiding the majority who exult in their new power."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CaptiveDoctors 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3065955245" "'It's science at gunpoint!'"
// DetailString :
"P4224977329" "When you rescued a scientist held captive by the anti-Nictus conspiracy within the council, he told you: <br><br>'By Fermat's last theorem, I thought I was done for until you arrived, {HeroName}! Those Council thugs have been holding myself and several other scientists captive, forcing us to work on new weapons under a man called Archon Swann. It's science at gunpoint! Fortunately, when Swann was captured, they didn't have anyone left who could tell what we were doing, so we were able to slow down our research without raising suspicion. They still have the others, but I'll help any way I can!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MovingScience 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P591777255" "Scientist Transfer Orders"
// DetailString :
"P3930838692" "You found these orders on Archon Swann's computer. They authorize the transfer of several captive scientists to another facility controlled by a fellow conspirator named Archon Stone. From the date, the move was very recent."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Leaderlist 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3379567902" "No honor among conspirators"
// DetailString :
"P2662554769" "You found this report on Archon Coster's body. It's shocking contents read: <br><br>My Lady:<br>I have the last name. As you suspected, it is Archon Stone. I transferred the scientists to his care, and now he trusts me completely. The full list of conspirators against you is: Voight, Stone, Saager, Turley, and Swann. With Swann's set-up and capture engineered so well, their technical progress has ground to a halt, and none of the remaining four suspect a thing. <br>As you surmised, My Lady, the Pantheon have begun to retaliate for the tests against them. I have purposefully played down this possibility to keep the others off guard. We shall soon be able to clean up the remainders. I would like to stress, however, that the Kheldians have been getting closer. We may need to deal with them soon. I await your next orders, Lady Arakhn. <br><br>Ever your servant, <br>Archon Coster'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TheCenterKnows 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4261757010" "'She told The Center everything'"
// DetailString :
"P3843655881" "After you defeated Lt. Wester, he told you: <br><br>'Arakhn knows that you're hunting down the conspirators. She's made plans to handle it. She told the Center everything. Even now his troops are preparing, soon they'll take care of all of the conspirators for us. Best of all, any accusations they make will look like desperate lies. You won't be able to move fast enough, Kheldian. They'll be out of your hands forever.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Evacuation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2827867593" "Evacuation plans"
// DetailString :
"P1906099701" "You found these plans on Archon Turley after you defeated them. It looks like the remaining conspirators think the cause is lost, and plan to take what they've learned and leave Striga Isle. What's more, they mention that they've made contact with another villain organization called  Arachnos, and plan to defect to it with all of their new weapons."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - VoightFinal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3429691692" "'Many, many more secrets...'"
// DetailString :
"P2627899424" "After you defeated Archon Voight, he said: <br><br>'You fought well. I can accept this loss, because I know that you'll keep fighting the Nictus even after I'm in the Ziggurat. The Council is a lost cause, though. Keep up your investigation. There are many more secrets than even we discovered. Many, many more secrets...'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2867025974" "Fear and Loathing on Striga Isle"
// DetailString :
"P4036267278" "After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P96966031" "After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them. <br><br>Searching for clues about why the Galaxy Archon Booker would help against the Kheldians, you investigated his old base. There you discovered that he had learned something dire about Arakhn's plans, and was feeling himself transforming into an alien being from his Nictus Fragment implants. These combined led him into the conspiracy."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P30991076" "After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them. <br><br>Searching for clues about why the Galaxy Archon Booker would help against the Kheldians, you investigated his old base. There you discovered that he had learned something dire about Arakhn's plans, and was feeling himself transforming into an alien being from his Nictus Fragment implants. These combined led him into the conspiracy. <br><br>One of the names mentioned in Booker's Journals was an Archon Coster, the head of a research base. You infiltrated the facility, but found it already under attack by the Banished Pantheon, who sought revenge for being used as test subjects. Coster had been killed by the Pantheon by the time you arrived, but his notes not only had the names of the remaining conspirators, but showed that Coster had been a double-agent, and had assembled those names for Arakhn herself!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1502573774" "After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them. <br><br>Searching for clues about why the Galaxy Archon Booker would help against the Kheldians, you investigated his old base. There you discovered that he had learned something dire about Arakhn's plans, and was feeling himself transforming into an alien being from his Nictus Fragment implants. These combined led him into the conspiracy. <br><br>One of the names mentioned in Booker's Journals was an Archon Coster, the head of a research base. You infiltrated the facility, but found it already under attack by the Banished Pantheon, who sought revenge for being used as test subjects. Coster had been killed by the Pantheon by the time you arrived, but his notes not only had the names of the remaining conspirators, but showed that Coster had been a double-agent, and had assembled those names for Arakhn herself! <br><br>You rescued the scientists that the Council Conspirators had forced to work on their anti-Nictus weapons, and captured Archon Stone, the third conspirator. From this point forward, it would be a race to capture the last conspirators before Arakhn could hunt them down."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4146538818" "After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them. <br><br>Searching for clues about why the Galaxy Archon Booker would help against the Kheldians, you investigated his old base. There you discovered that he had learned something dire about Arakhn's plans, and was feeling himself transforming into an alien being from his Nictus Fragment implants. These combined led him into the conspiracy. <br><br>One of the names mentioned in Booker's Journals was an Archon Coster, the head of a research base. You infiltrated the facility, but found it already under attack by the Banished Pantheon, who sought revenge for being used as test subjects. Coster had been killed by the Pantheon by the time you arrived, but his notes not only had the names of the remaining conspirators, but showed that Coster had been a double-agent, and had assembled those names for Arakhn herself! <br><br>You rescued the scientists that the Council Conspirators had forced to work on their anti-Nictus weapons, and captured Archon Stone, the third conspirator. From this point forward, it would be a race to capture the last conspirators before Arakhn could hunt them down. <br><br>You captured Lt. Wester and Archon Turley, two more members of the conspiracy, before Arakhn could assassinate them. You also discovered that the remaining conspirators planned to escape Striga Island and defect to another organization."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL5_Kheldian_Storyarc1_Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3730686645" "A prototype Quantum weapon"
// tDetailString :
"P795879062" "Dr. Winslowe and his team and SERAPH gave you this non-functional prototype, based on designs captured from a conspiracy within the Council itself. Winslowe thinks he may be able to perfect the design one day, but for now you keep it as a memento of the strange case you remember as: <br><br>Fear and Loathing on Striga Isle <br><br>After a captured Council Archon had revealed the existence of a rabidly anti-Nictus and anti-Kheldian faction within the Council, monitoring of the evil organization was stepped up dramatically, looking for further clues. The clue you were looking for came when Moonfire, the Kheldian agent on Striga Island, discovered that a group of Council Soldiers was secretly testing new weapons against the Banished Pantheon. The weapons were being tuned for use against Nictus, but you found both a War Wolf and a Galaxy soldier working to help test them. <br><br>Searching for clues about why the Galaxy Archon Booker would help against the Kheldians, you investigated his old base. There you discovered that he had learned something dire about Arakhn's plans, and was feeling himself transforming into an alien being from his Nictus Fragment implants. These combined led him into the conspiracy. <br><br>One of the names mentioned in Booker's Journals was an Archon Coster, the head of a research base. You infiltrated the facility, but found it already under attack by the Banished Pantheon, who sought revenge for being used as test subjects. Coster had been killed by the Pantheon by the time you arrived, but his notes not only had the names of the remaining conspirators, but showed that Coster had been a double-agent, and had assembled those names for Arakhn herself! <br><br>You rescued the scientists that the Council Conspirators had forced to work on their anti-Nictus weapons, and captured Archon Stone, the third conspirator. From this point forward, it would be a race to capture the last conspirators before Arakhn could hunt them down. <br><br>You captured Lt. Wester and Archon Turley, two more members of the conspiracy, before Arakhn could assassinate them. You also discovered that the remaining conspirators planned to escape Striga Island and defect to another organization. <br><br>As you rushed the capture the last two conspirators for all of the valuable information they held, you learned that Arakhn had alerted the Center to conspiracy. With no time to lose, you captured Archon Saager and Archon Voight before they could escape from Striga on a Cargo vessel. With all the conspirators safely captured, Arakhn's attempts to assassinate them were foiled, and much new information about Nictus activity within the Council could be gained. <br>It may take some time for the conspirators to talk, so you were encouraged to improve your powers until then so you'd be ready to investigate whatever was revealed. You were told to come back when you were about Stature Level 30 to continue."

